WEBVTT

00:06.820 --> 00:08.610
Welcome back, Professor.

00:09.640 --> 00:12.090
How did your lunch meeting 
with Lord Fennel go?

00:16.020 --> 00:18.940
You look upset. Was there a problem?

00:19.920 --> 00:24.840
Do you really think I'd cause a problem 
during a lunch with Lord Fennel?

00:25.540 --> 00:27.750
No, sir. I apologize.

00:31.410 --> 00:34.090
I'd like you to examine 
my daughter, Professor.

00:34.090 --> 00:37.520
A week ago, she developed 
a rash on her face.

00:37.520 --> 00:39.980
I assumed it would get better on its own,

00:39.980 --> 00:43.350
but it seems to be getting bigger over time.

00:43.580 --> 00:46.980
That may be a case of Odd Face.

00:47.360 --> 00:48.860
Odd Face?

00:49.330 --> 00:51.980
Professor, is there 
anything that can be done?

00:52.320 --> 00:54.510
I owe you so much already!

00:54.510 --> 00:56.490
I'm sure you can manage this.

00:57.500 --> 00:59.460
<i>It's not life-threatening,</i>

00:59.460 --> 01:02.160
<i>but if the growth is at 
the point that it's visible,</i>

01:02.160 --> 01:04.750
<i>that means it's taken root deep already.</i>

01:04.750 --> 01:10.750
<i>Considering the amount of cutting that will 
be necessary, it's likely to leave a scar.</i>

01:11.010 --> 01:14.770
<i>With enough donors and 
health transfer magic,</i>

01:14.770 --> 01:18.340
<i>the skin can be regenerated 
without trouble...</i>

01:18.340 --> 01:21.540
<i>but Lord Fennel said his daughter 
would absolutely refuse</i>

01:21.540 --> 01:23.690
<i>to let too many people see her face.</i>

01:24.680 --> 01:27.700
<i>I can count on one assistant, 
maybe two at most.</i>

01:32.210 --> 01:33.360
<i>At times like this,</i>

01:33.360 --> 01:35.900
<i>it's best to soothe my nerves 
by gazing at my dear Milk.</i>

01:43.530 --> 01:46.620
I heard your darling pup 
got run over by a carriage.

01:46.620 --> 01:47.750
What?!

01:48.620 --> 01:51.010
Are you behind this?!

01:51.010 --> 01:53.500
It's about time you learned your place!

01:53.500 --> 01:56.950
It wasn't me. And I don't 
appreciate the insinuation.

01:56.950 --> 02:02.220
Besides, I heard the dog-sitter healed 
her and she's all better, anyway.

02:08.520 --> 02:10.640
<i>I confirmed with my secretary on the way,</i>

02:10.640 --> 02:12.770
<i>and it seems she really was in an accident.</i>

02:17.920 --> 02:23.520
<i>Someone capable of healing an injury 
completely, with no trace of scarring...</i>

02:26.560 --> 02:28.870
Good girl, good girl!

02:46.060 --> 02:53.570
<b>The Brilliant Healer's
New Life in the Shadows</b>

04:02.970 --> 04:04.590
I'm in a real bind here!

04:04.590 --> 04:06.430
Please help me!

04:10.720 --> 04:13.850
I was asked to heal the daughter 
of one of the seven major nobles.

04:13.850 --> 04:15.570
You know about Odd Face, right?

04:15.570 --> 04:17.320
She's come down with that.

04:17.320 --> 04:18.540
Don't tell anyone!

04:18.540 --> 04:19.980
You just told us...

04:19.980 --> 04:23.010
Why the panic? If it's a benign growth, 
she could leave it and be perfectly fine.

04:23.010 --> 04:25.080
Even I know that!

04:25.080 --> 04:28.700
But she won't attend any of her social 
functions with that thing on her face!

04:28.700 --> 04:30.380
Then why not cut it out?

04:30.380 --> 04:33.330
It's rooted too deep. 
The excision would cover a huge area!

04:33.330 --> 04:36.090
Even textbooks say the scarring is so bad

04:36.090 --> 04:38.840
that Odd Face is better left untreated!

04:38.840 --> 04:43.360
If I mess up the face of one of 
the seven nobles, I'm done for!

04:43.360 --> 04:46.340
Why don't you just make 
sure there's no scar, then?

04:47.030 --> 04:50.600
Talking to you always makes 
me question my sanity...

04:50.600 --> 04:53.700
It's not that easy for 
normal people, you know!

04:53.700 --> 04:58.110
I'm curious as to why such a lofty 
request was made of <i>you</i>, Cresson.

04:59.490 --> 05:03.610
Because Professor Goldran has finally 
realized how brilliant I am!

05:06.570 --> 05:09.760
That's a lie! Don't give 
me that frosty look!

05:09.760 --> 05:11.450
Aren't we classmates?!

05:11.450 --> 05:15.060
The professor asked for me after 
what happened with Madam Milk!

05:15.060 --> 05:16.950
So, just like with the zombie king,

05:16.950 --> 05:19.340
you stole the credit for something?

05:19.340 --> 05:20.680
It's not like that.

05:20.680 --> 05:25.100
I told the second secretary that the 
special research student handled it.

05:25.100 --> 05:27.800
You could always just tell him 
that was the case again,

05:27.800 --> 05:29.590
and admit that you were totally useless.

05:29.590 --> 05:32.470
You're weirdly harsh on me,
considering we're classmates!

05:32.470 --> 05:35.270
Besides, if I tell them it wasn't me again,

05:35.270 --> 05:38.330
the second secretary is gonna 
notice and write me off.

05:38.850 --> 05:42.730
So, that being the case, 
I need your help, bro!

05:42.730 --> 05:45.110
I'm not your bro.

05:47.200 --> 05:48.950
I made some tea.

05:48.950 --> 05:50.010
Who's this?

05:50.010 --> 05:52.200
Zeno's little sister.

05:52.200 --> 05:55.580
Thank you for always 
looking after my brother.

05:55.580 --> 05:58.580
Wouldn't have expected you 
to have such a cute sister...

05:58.580 --> 06:00.260
Cute?

06:01.590 --> 06:03.710
I'm so sorry,

06:03.710 --> 06:05.710
but I belong to my big brother.

06:05.710 --> 06:08.970
So no matter how much you compliment 
me, I'll never be yours, Cresson.

06:08.970 --> 06:10.840
Not even a "Mister" Cresson?!

06:10.840 --> 06:13.730
And you two are <i>that</i> kind of siblings, huh?

06:13.730 --> 06:15.600
No, we're not.

06:15.600 --> 06:19.990
Still, if you're my bro's sister, 
you're basically mine, too.

06:19.990 --> 06:21.600
Nice to meet you, little sis!

06:21.600 --> 06:22.980
That's also wrong.

06:24.040 --> 06:26.610
I don't want a big brother like him!

06:34.330 --> 06:37.450
Professor, we've been waiting for you.

06:37.450 --> 06:41.710
Lord Fennel, why the sudden summons?

06:41.710 --> 06:45.870
Well... the situation's 
become a bit complicated.

06:48.120 --> 06:52.390
It seems that Charlotte 
is refusing the surgery.

06:52.390 --> 06:54.780
She's locked herself in 
her room, saying that

06:54.780 --> 06:57.350
any kind of scar on her 
face is unacceptable.

06:57.350 --> 06:59.030
I see.

06:59.030 --> 07:04.560
But I have faith that you can treat 
her without leaving a scar, Professor!

07:04.560 --> 07:06.730
Yes, of course.

07:06.730 --> 07:11.200
So would you please convince my daughter?

07:11.200 --> 07:12.650
Understood.

07:21.330 --> 07:24.460
Charlotte, the professor is here.

07:26.710 --> 07:28.050
It's me, Papa.

07:28.050 --> 07:30.970
You should let the professor 
handle your treatment.

07:30.970 --> 07:34.780
It'll be fine. Have I ever lied to you?

07:40.600 --> 07:45.330
Papa, you promised me that that 
fire fox pelt scarf for my birthday,

07:45.330 --> 07:46.860
but you didn't get it for me!

07:50.030 --> 07:54.510
Miss, my name is Goldran. 
I'm with the royal hospital.

07:54.510 --> 07:57.800
Would you be willing to trust 
me to treat your condition?

07:57.800 --> 07:58.700
No!

07:58.700 --> 08:02.540
But without surgery, 
your condition can't be fixed.

08:02.540 --> 08:05.510
I absolutely refuse to allow 
a blade near my face!

08:05.510 --> 08:09.290
I bet you were ordered by someone to 
mutilate my beautiful face, weren't you?!

08:09.290 --> 08:10.670
Of course not!

08:10.670 --> 08:12.480
I bet it's the Geese family's girl.

08:12.480 --> 08:17.280
She's always been jealous of me.
She probably arranged this whole thing.

08:17.280 --> 08:19.500
I guess being too pretty 
brings its own problems.

08:20.670 --> 08:21.880
Hey, bro.

08:21.880 --> 08:23.760
I'm not your bro, but what?

08:23.760 --> 08:26.320
I just had an awesome idea.

08:26.320 --> 08:29.070
Something even simpler 
than getting promoted.

08:29.070 --> 08:33.680
Say I convince her to go under the knife, 
we heal her perfectly, and she falls for me...

08:33.680 --> 08:35.340
Then we get married.

08:36.280 --> 08:40.310
All of a sudden, I'm a member of 
the aristocracy! It's a perfect plan.

08:40.310 --> 08:42.460
Yeah? Hope that works for you.

08:43.790 --> 08:45.610
Let me speak to her, please!

08:47.520 --> 08:50.330
Excuse me, Miss Charlotte?

08:50.330 --> 08:51.820
And who are you?

08:51.820 --> 08:55.370
My name is Cresson. 
I'm the professor's assistant.

08:55.370 --> 08:56.680
What?

08:56.680 --> 08:59.650
Where does some assistant 
get off talking to me?

08:59.650 --> 09:01.100
You're noise pollution!

09:01.100 --> 09:02.930
S-Sorry!

09:03.680 --> 09:07.380
Bro! I'm gonna work my 
way to the top after all!

09:07.380 --> 09:09.210
You can't trust chicks.

09:09.210 --> 09:11.360
You sure know how to adapt, huh?

09:14.680 --> 09:15.870
<i>Guess it's my turn.</i>

09:19.410 --> 09:22.290
Uh, can you hear me?

09:22.560 --> 09:23.650
Another one?

09:24.160 --> 09:25.600
Who are you?

09:25.600 --> 09:28.000
You certainly seem to be lacking in manners.

09:28.000 --> 09:29.920
I'm the other assistant.

09:29.920 --> 09:31.840
Again?! Where does some assistant get off—

09:31.840 --> 09:35.170
About the surgery. If you don't 
want to do it, that's fine.

09:37.130 --> 09:40.640
Anyone would be scared to have 
their face cut open with a knife.

09:40.640 --> 09:42.860
And that growth won't kill you,

09:42.860 --> 09:44.970
so there's no need to force 
it if you don't want to.

09:44.970 --> 09:46.640
It's your call to make.

09:46.640 --> 09:50.040
Left alone, the worst you'll have is a 
mark that looks like an old lady's face.

09:50.040 --> 09:52.770
Some people even get 
attached to how they look.

09:52.770 --> 09:55.520
They even give the growths 
names and everything.

09:56.980 --> 09:58.980
Well, that does it for me.

09:58.980 --> 10:00.410
What do you think you're doing?!

10:04.010 --> 10:05.610
W-Wait.

10:07.690 --> 10:09.160
Just wait...

10:13.030 --> 10:17.590
Oh, wow! Pictures that were 
produced with a magic projector!

10:17.590 --> 10:19.810
Do you know how expensive 
it is to get these in color?!

10:19.810 --> 10:21.550
These folks really are rich!

10:22.480 --> 10:24.720
So, is that true?

10:24.720 --> 10:28.030
If nothing is done, the growth will 
look like an old woman's face?

10:28.600 --> 10:30.740
Yes, that's right! It's—

10:30.740 --> 10:32.730
Keep your mouth shut.

10:32.730 --> 10:35.860
I don't want your breath 
stinking up my lovely room.

10:39.880 --> 10:42.290
Yes, it is true, milady.

10:42.290 --> 10:46.240
It's called Odd Face, and after about a month,

10:46.240 --> 10:49.250
the growth takes the shape 
of an old woman's face.

10:49.590 --> 10:51.880
So, what do I do?!

10:51.880 --> 10:54.880
The only way to remove it is via surgery.

10:54.880 --> 10:55.980
I refuse to be cut!

10:55.980 --> 10:56.880
But—

10:56.880 --> 10:59.260
I won't be cut! I don't want pain!

10:59.260 --> 11:01.120
And I don't want the growth to stay!

11:01.120 --> 11:03.010
I don't want any of this!

11:03.010 --> 11:05.760
This chick is spoiled like crazy.

11:05.760 --> 11:10.010
Charlotte, if we don't do something, 
the growth will only get bigger.

11:10.010 --> 11:12.690
Why not trust the professor 
to take care of it?

11:12.690 --> 11:15.950
You don't care if my face 
is all scarred up, Papa?

11:15.950 --> 11:19.580
It won't be! The professor 
can heal the scars.

11:19.580 --> 11:20.990
Can you guarantee that?!

11:20.990 --> 11:22.530
Guarantee...

11:24.440 --> 11:27.910
I refuse unless you can guarantee 
me there will be no scars!

11:29.600 --> 11:31.230
Charlotte...

11:45.000 --> 11:46.460
You like birds, huh?

11:47.680 --> 11:51.490
Why is another assistant talking to me?

11:51.490 --> 11:54.460
You're fouling the air of 
my room with your breath.

11:54.460 --> 11:57.190
We're on the veranda, 
so I'm pretty sure I'm not.

11:58.210 --> 11:59.530
You think you're so clever.

12:00.770 --> 12:02.460
One of them is hurt.

12:07.160 --> 12:09.420
I found it in the garden yesterday.

12:09.920 --> 12:11.370
It won't be able to fly again...

12:12.640 --> 12:13.920
just like me.

12:15.030 --> 12:19.190
No more dresses for me. Or dancing at balls.

12:19.190 --> 12:22.010
It won't be long before people 
ignore me altogether.

12:22.720 --> 12:25.050
Do you want to get better?

12:25.370 --> 12:27.680
Just stop talking to me.

12:28.000 --> 12:31.560
I'll ask again. Do you want 
your illness to get better?

12:31.860 --> 12:35.410
Of course I do! But I don't want any scars!

12:35.410 --> 12:37.600
So stop talking to me!

12:37.600 --> 12:39.650
Who do you think I am?!

12:39.650 --> 12:40.620
A patient.

12:43.280 --> 12:47.740
If you're in trouble and request 
treatment, you're a patient.

12:48.490 --> 12:53.000
I don't care if you're royalty, 
nobility, a civilian, or a peasant.

12:53.410 --> 12:56.250
Healing patients is my job.

13:01.880 --> 13:04.010
You want to dance again, right?

13:05.560 --> 13:06.880
Well, he flew.

13:08.100 --> 13:09.380
I...

13:10.720 --> 13:12.960
Can I fly again?

13:13.830 --> 13:15.660
If you want to, yeah.

13:23.490 --> 13:26.510
Please, take good care of her, Professor.

13:29.340 --> 13:32.740
<i>Did Becker make this sleeping drug, too?</i>

13:33.430 --> 13:36.040
All right, time for you two to go to work.

13:36.620 --> 13:39.030
This absolutely has to be a success.

13:39.030 --> 13:43.270
I'm sure you realize what'll 
happen if you fail.

13:43.270 --> 13:45.850
R-Right! Leave it to me!

13:48.340 --> 13:50.040
I'll handle the surgery.

13:50.040 --> 13:52.320
Bro, have you done this before?

13:52.320 --> 13:53.710
When I was a kid, yeah.

13:53.710 --> 13:54.930
Huh?

13:54.930 --> 13:56.180
Don't worry about it.

13:56.180 --> 13:59.230
Point is, I have some experience, 
so I should be able to manage.

13:59.230 --> 14:02.010
I really picked the right guy for my big bro!

14:02.010 --> 14:03.860
I never agreed to that, you know.

14:05.660 --> 14:07.780
What are you doing?

14:07.780 --> 14:11.710
Dog-sitter, you were the one 
who treated Milk, right?

14:11.710 --> 14:13.450
You'll be the surgeon.

14:13.990 --> 14:16.060
Uh, but...

14:16.060 --> 14:17.110
What is it?

14:18.020 --> 14:20.380
Nothing, sir.

14:20.380 --> 14:22.010
Then get started already!

14:22.010 --> 14:22.780
Yes, sir.

14:27.550 --> 14:30.100
So that's what most people 
use for the incisions?

14:30.100 --> 14:32.470
What else would you use?

14:32.470 --> 14:36.610
Come on, if you keep shaking like that, 
it's only gonna leave a bigger scar.

14:36.610 --> 14:39.850
Don't worry. It's not a 
complicated procedure.

14:39.850 --> 14:42.960
The textbook says it's A+ difficulty!

14:42.960 --> 14:44.110
Hey!

14:44.110 --> 14:45.990
What are you babbling about?

14:45.990 --> 14:47.340
R-Right.

14:48.280 --> 14:53.610
<i>The roots of Odd Face growths are said 
to take hold at 3, 7, and 10 o'clock...</i>

14:53.610 --> 14:54.990
One sec.

14:54.990 --> 14:55.940
Scan.

14:57.060 --> 14:58.560
What was that?

14:58.560 --> 15:00.500
I ran an internal check.

15:00.500 --> 15:02.450
The directions of the roots can vary,

15:02.450 --> 15:04.760
so you shouldn't assume 
common knowledge is correct.

15:04.760 --> 15:09.380
In this case, 2, 6, 9, and 10 o'clock.

15:09.380 --> 15:11.210
You can tell all that?

15:11.210 --> 15:13.540
Can't operate unless you can.

15:13.540 --> 15:16.600
I'll whisper the specifics 
to you, so just do as I say.

15:16.600 --> 15:17.980
Bro!

15:35.380 --> 15:38.310
I'm impressed, dog-sitter.

15:38.310 --> 15:39.530
Oh, no...

15:39.530 --> 15:40.790
What is it?

15:41.080 --> 15:44.040
Well... the roots... are 
tangled with her nerves.

15:44.630 --> 15:46.980
To cut them, I'd have to cut the nerves, too—

15:46.980 --> 15:47.920
Hold on!

15:47.920 --> 15:50.030
Doing that will alter her appearance.

15:50.030 --> 15:53.390
Nerves are a lot harder 
to repair than epidermis.

15:53.390 --> 15:56.490
B-But if we leave any roots uncut, 
the growth will come back!

15:56.490 --> 15:58.400
Maybe we should close her up and try to

15:58.400 --> 16:01.140
convince her to undergo a second 
surgery at the royal hospital?

16:01.140 --> 16:03.390
It's too late for that!

16:03.390 --> 16:08.590
If we don't deal with the growth now, it'll 
likely grow back even stronger than before!

16:11.650 --> 16:13.240
We've no choice.

16:13.240 --> 16:14.060
Cut it out.

16:14.530 --> 16:16.780
Y-You're sure?

16:16.780 --> 16:21.550
Leaving a root behind and the resulting
recurrence will reflect badly on my reputation.

16:21.550 --> 16:24.290
Our priority is completely 
removing the growth.

16:24.290 --> 16:27.250
But it'll change her appearance!

16:27.250 --> 16:29.940
This is bound to affect 
the director's election,

16:29.940 --> 16:32.960
but leaving the root will 
end up disfiguring her.

16:32.960 --> 16:36.220
The best choice here is 
to minimize the damage.

16:37.970 --> 16:41.730
<i>Damn it! I can't believe
I got stuck with this mess.</i>

16:46.770 --> 16:48.550
You imbecile!

16:50.230 --> 16:52.360
How could you do this?!

16:52.360 --> 16:54.240
Is something wrong, Professor?

16:54.240 --> 16:59.800
My idiot assistant ignored 
my orders and cut her nerves!

16:59.800 --> 17:02.750
I said that was the one thing not to do!

17:05.250 --> 17:07.360
Is that a problem?

17:07.360 --> 17:09.120
A major one!

17:09.120 --> 17:11.860
And it's your fault, dog-sitter!

17:11.860 --> 17:15.610
Since we have no other choice, we'll 
take her to the royal hospital tomorrow,

17:15.610 --> 17:19.970
and I'll reconnect the nerves 
with my health transfer magic.

17:19.970 --> 17:22.200
It won't restore her completely,

17:22.200 --> 17:24.530
but it should be better 
than her current state.

17:25.940 --> 17:27.260
Don't worry about it.

17:28.230 --> 17:32.710
The nerves just had to be cut because the 
roots of the growth were running too deep.

17:32.710 --> 17:34.610
You just need to reconnect what was cut.

17:35.040 --> 17:37.620
I don't need to worry?

17:37.620 --> 17:39.740
My daughter will be fine, then?

17:39.740 --> 17:41.990
Yeah, she will be.

17:41.990 --> 17:44.780
An injury like this is 
nothing to worry about.

17:44.780 --> 17:48.250
And definitely nothing worth 
going to the royal hospital for.

17:48.250 --> 17:50.220
Wouldn't you agree, Professor?

17:50.220 --> 17:51.540
What?

17:52.650 --> 17:54.840
This girl said she wanted to dance again.

17:54.840 --> 17:57.800
She was scared, but willing to trust us.

17:57.800 --> 18:00.840
As a healer, I need to answer that.

18:02.790 --> 18:05.700
All right, I'm getting a little 
tired of standing around.

18:05.700 --> 18:07.200
It's time to wrap this up.

18:18.440 --> 18:20.120
<i>You did great.</i>

18:20.970 --> 18:22.820
<i>The surgery was a success.</i>

18:30.780 --> 18:32.320
Charlotte!

18:31.510 --> 18:33.630
Wait, Papa.

18:33.630 --> 18:34.880
A mirror...

18:36.620 --> 18:40.000
Papa... The growth is gone?

18:40.000 --> 18:43.100
Yes. They were able to completely remove it!

18:44.820 --> 18:46.130
Thank goodness...

18:47.030 --> 18:48.310
I'm so glad.

18:49.360 --> 18:51.350
It really is a relief!

18:51.350 --> 18:54.380
Professor Goldran did a perfect job.

18:54.380 --> 18:55.580
Yes...

18:56.290 --> 18:57.380
Where is he?

18:57.380 --> 19:02.830
He seems to be busy with the upcoming 
election for hospital director,

19:02.830 --> 19:06.120
and I didn't want to keep 
him, so I let him go.

19:06.120 --> 19:07.580
I see...

19:07.580 --> 19:11.620
I do, of course, intend to offer him
my full support in the election.

19:11.620 --> 19:13.250
After all, he saved me once,

19:13.250 --> 19:15.630
and now he's saved you, as well.

19:15.630 --> 19:17.470
R-Right.

19:18.130 --> 19:19.670
<i>You did great.</i>

19:21.750 --> 19:25.440
Say, Papa... What was his name?

19:25.440 --> 19:26.510
Whose?

19:26.510 --> 19:28.850
The one with bad manners!

19:28.850 --> 19:34.610
Oh, the professor's second 
assistant? What of him?

19:34.610 --> 19:37.110
Wh-What difference does it make?

19:37.110 --> 19:42.530
Miss, I believe his name was Zeno.

19:50.840 --> 19:51.900
Zeno...

19:58.660 --> 20:01.130
I appreciate you helping me out.

20:01.370 --> 20:03.710
It's fine, but this is a lot of bottles.

20:03.710 --> 20:05.350
What's in them?

20:05.350 --> 20:07.670
These are experimental 
concoctions of Dr. Becker's.

20:07.670 --> 20:09.720
We're moving them into storage.

20:11.180 --> 20:12.800
What kind of drug is it?

20:12.800 --> 20:14.290
That's a good question.

20:14.290 --> 20:16.020
You don't know?

20:17.150 --> 20:20.140
I'm not sure Dr. Becker knows, either.

20:20.140 --> 20:21.830
Shouldn't he, though?

20:23.120 --> 20:25.600
Well, he always says 
repeated experimentation

20:25.600 --> 20:29.330
holds the promise of new breakthroughs.

20:29.640 --> 20:34.560
I just wish he'd consider I feel as the one 
who has to find a way to store the results.

20:34.560 --> 20:36.460
I am grateful, though.

20:36.940 --> 20:38.460
Dr. Becker.

20:38.460 --> 20:41.440
You didn't have to carry them all at once.

20:41.440 --> 20:45.800
I wanted to make sure they were stored 
in the best condition possible.

20:46.080 --> 20:47.820
I appreciate that.

20:47.820 --> 20:51.600
These concoctions are going to be 
particularly valuable this time.

20:51.600 --> 20:54.060
You say that every time.

20:54.060 --> 20:55.840
Do I?

20:56.520 --> 20:59.070
How did your noble surgery go?

20:59.070 --> 21:00.440
Well enough.

21:00.440 --> 21:02.570
I suppose I didn't need to ask.

21:02.570 --> 21:06.120
Maybe now Professor Goldran 
will think highly of you.

21:06.120 --> 21:07.840
Bro!

21:08.450 --> 21:14.710
You and I were invited to one of 
Professor Goldran's dinner parties!

21:15.750 --> 21:17.420
Zeno, that's amazing!

21:17.420 --> 21:19.880
Congratulations, Zeno.

21:21.590 --> 21:25.360
Normally, you'd get a big head
and make snide remarks.

21:25.360 --> 21:26.680
What's going on?

21:26.680 --> 21:28.400
Aren't you glad?

21:28.400 --> 21:30.870
I mean, I am, but...

21:31.310 --> 21:33.560
You could be selected to be an officer!

21:33.560 --> 21:36.560
This is the opportunity for a promotion 
that you've been waiting for!

21:36.870 --> 21:39.580
Yeah... That's right!

21:41.940 --> 21:45.820
Once I become a big shot, 
I'll push you around!

21:46.090 --> 21:49.570
Now there's the friendless 
Cresson I remember!

21:49.570 --> 21:51.400
Don't call me friendless!

21:51.400 --> 21:54.200
I'm pretty self-conscious about that!

21:54.200 --> 21:56.400
Let's get a move on, bro!

21:56.400 --> 21:58.240
The dinner party is this evening,

21:58.240 --> 22:00.330
so I'll see you in the lobby tonight!

22:01.840 --> 22:04.440
He's taken a real liking to you.

22:04.440 --> 22:07.090
I'm not thrilled about it.

22:07.090 --> 22:10.180
Whatever the case, congratulations.

22:10.180 --> 22:13.300
I don't think anyone has 
ever been invited to one of

22:13.300 --> 22:16.020
Professor Goldran's dinner 
parties in such a short time.

22:16.020 --> 22:19.780
The risk I took in bringing you into 
this matter is really paying off.

22:20.790 --> 22:23.480
Your job is almost done.

23:55.530 --> 24:00.000
Just a Normal Healer

23:57.180 --> 23:58.620
"Just a Normal Healer."
